================================== Descent consistency read-off (symbolic, no new assumptions) ==================================
  old hypotenuse c       =  m**2 + n**2
  new hypotenuse c'      =  m
  gap c - c'             =  m**2 - m + n**2
  so each descent step lowers the positive integer c  ->  c'  by a gap (c-c') = (m-1)m+n^2 >= 1;
  an infinite strictly-decreasing chain of positive integers cannot exist.

